Author: HACKER CAT (tm)

FelineWare... Improve it and gimme credits! :)
Release 1.0 - Unregistered, but Unregistrable =D

Sorry for the DOCS! :) I think AMIGAGUIDE docs are a pain in the (you know)
when configuring CNET :) :) :)

        Here in Mexico there are more users that think that they need a very
easy menu to use the BBS. I have made about 140+ MODs to my BBS for making it
easy to use. The newest is this: a QWK menu, that is accesible from the BASE
menu, and it works really neat!!!



Installing.
-----------
Copy the puny little script into PFILES:. That's it. Now, just you need to
modify ONE line in your BBSmenu so it can work. Here, down, is the copy of my
BBS menu BASE section:


4; ud/base
	SN~Scan NEW
	RN~Read NEW PREVIEW
	YN~Yank NEW PREVIEW
	BN~Browse NEW PREVIEW
	SA~SG NEW
	RA~RG NEW PREVIEW
	QWKO~YG NEW PREVIEW <- The expert user just uses QWKO to download QWK
	BA~BG NEW
	AL, Add List
	KL, Kill List
	EL, Edit List
	YG, Yank Global
	SG, Scan Global
	RG, Read Global
	BG, Browse Global
	VIew
	Again
	Browse
	Download
	Examine
	TYPE,Grab
	DRop
	Join
	Kill,DELete
	List
	NOTE,NEw
	Off,LOGOFF
	Post
	Read
	DIR,Scan
	Quit
	Upload
	Validate
	AO, Adopt Orphans
	ENtry
	*
	?
	<
	>
	/
	Write
	ATtribute
	MOve
	REspond
	Z, SEArch
	ZG, SEArch Global
	Yank
	Xit
	:
	ML
	TEst
	TRansform
	INvite
	ORder
	CD
	EDit
	VOte
	RR
	CArbon
	MEmbers
        QWK | *0 pfiles:QWK} <- here it is the modification!
              ^ ya know, the CTRL-Q

Now, rename your CNET QWK command to REP .... that's it. So, if a user wants
to upload it's REP in a hurry, he (or she) just enters REP and that's it, the
BBS will prompt the user to upload it's REP packet.

Wooow! This thingie really works great, so start by translating it better
than I did, because my English it's no so good =]


2.63 SYSOPS
-----------

If you are operating a 2.63 board, you will need to modify the script where
it says "REP". Modify it to:

q!;u!;{the # of your REP board};u!

it will work not so neat as 3.05C, but it will work =]... so, why not getting
the PRO upgrade (the other CNET down here is not a 24 hour BBS and has waited
over a YEAR to it's upgrade!)

SUGGESTIONS
-----------

I suggest that in your SYS.ENTRY of your BASE, post a phrase like...

           "Use the QWK Command to Enter The QWK MENU!"

